  "question": {
    "text": "<p>List I contains four combinations of two lenses (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>) whose focal lengths (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>) are indicated in the figures. In all cases, the object is placed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mi>cm</mi></math> from the first lens on the left, and the distance between the two lenses is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>cm</mi></math>. List II contains the positions of the final images.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>List-I</strong></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>List-II</strong></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(I)</td>\t\t\t<td><img src=\"assets\\qt0010_e5060956c671.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 116px;\" /></td>\t\t\t<td>(P)</td>\t\t\t<td>\t\t\t<p>Final image is formed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>cm</mi></math> on the&nbsp;right side of lens <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>\t\t\t</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(II)</td>\t\t\t<td><img src=\"assets\\qt0010_b60a869574f5.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 108px;\" /></td>\t\t\t<td>(Q)</td>\t\t\t<td>\t\t\t<p>Final image is formed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>cm</mi></math> on the&nbsp;right side of lens <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>\t\t\t</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(III)</td>\t\t\t<td><img src=\"assets\\qt0010_c683ba8d5aae.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 112px;\" /></td>\t\t\t<td>(R)</td>\t\t\t<td>\t\t\t<p>Final image is formed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>cm</mi></math> on the&nbsp;left side of lens <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>\t\t\t</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(IV)</td>\t\t\t<td><img src=\"assets\\qt0010_351c23a2d451.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 123px;\" /></td>\t\t\t<td>(S)</td>\t\t\t<td>\t\t\t<p>Final image is formed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>cm</mi></math> on the&nbsp;right side of lens <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>\t\t\t</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>(T)</td>\t\t\t<td>Final image is formed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>cm</mi></math> on the right side of lens <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Which one of the following options is correct?</p>"
  },
